WEBVTT

00:00:13.450 --> 00:00:16.140
Ko, your alarm's been ringing forever!

00:00:16.140 --> 00:00:17.800
Wake up already!

00:00:24.110 --> 00:00:25.470
Ko!

00:00:44.790 --> 00:00:46.990
What's up, Kitamura!

00:00:46.990 --> 00:00:48.350
It's me, Senda Keiichiro.

00:00:48.350 --> 00:00:53.100
Seishu Academy Middle School baseball team's ace pitcher and cleanup hitter.

00:00:53.100 --> 00:00:55.720
You look as shabby as ever.

00:00:55.720 --> 00:00:57.740
At least fix your bed head.

00:00:57.740 --> 00:01:00.280
That's why you're not getting any, man.

00:01:00.280 --> 00:01:01.940
Go away.

00:01:02.320 --> 00:01:04.380
Hey, Tsukishima!

00:01:06.010 --> 00:01:07.610
It's me, Senda Keiichiro!

00:01:07.610 --> 00:01:12.450
Seishu Academy Middle School baseball team's ace pitcher and cleanup hitter.

00:02:48.280 --> 00:02:52.180
I Hate Him!

00:03:04.530 --> 00:03:06.500
No way, stop lying!

00:03:06.500 --> 00:03:09.350
I'm not lying, seriously!

00:03:10.530 --> 00:03:13.080
Come on over, Kitamura!

00:03:13.080 --> 00:03:15.630
I'll at least introduce you to one of my fans.

00:03:15.630 --> 00:03:17.310
As a gesture of friendship.

00:03:17.310 --> 00:03:18.280
Friendship?

00:03:18.280 --> 00:03:20.350
It'll do you some good, man.

00:03:20.350 --> 00:03:24.350
After all, girls <i>are</i> the only thing healthy ninth-grade boys like us think about.

00:03:24.350 --> 00:03:26.110
Speak for yourself.

00:03:27.320 --> 00:03:29.310
You'll regret saying that!

00:03:29.310 --> 00:03:33.090
Get on my bad side and you'll have all the girls in school to answer to.

00:03:33.090 --> 00:03:35.090
Get on Ko's bad side,

00:03:35.090 --> 00:03:37.530
and you'll have us to answer to.

00:03:39.270 --> 00:03:42.460
We're going to have a practice game against Fourth Middle School the day after tomorrow.

00:03:42.460 --> 00:03:43.870
Would you guys like to come and root for—

00:03:43.870 --> 00:03:45.000
In your dreams.

00:03:45.000 --> 00:03:46.230
Oh, I see.

00:03:46.230 --> 00:03:47.830
I guess you're all busy.

00:03:47.830 --> 00:03:48.740
No, we're free.

00:03:48.740 --> 00:03:51.050
W-Well, then...

00:03:51.050 --> 00:03:54.180
I've got practice, so I'll see you around, Kitamura!

00:03:54.560 --> 00:03:56.080
Worthless punk.

00:03:56.430 --> 00:03:59.990
But he's our team's best pitcher and cleanup hitter right now, isn't he?

00:03:59.990 --> 00:04:02.190
Right now he is.

00:04:02.190 --> 00:04:05.850
But none of the good high schools are scouting him.

00:04:05.850 --> 00:04:07.690
That shows how good he is.

00:04:10.130 --> 00:04:11.930
But <i>she</i> is the real deal.

00:04:17.410 --> 00:04:21.390
It's too bad she can only play in official games until the end of middle school.

00:04:22.310 --> 00:04:24.240
Not bad, Tsukishima.

00:04:24.240 --> 00:04:25.440
Not bad at all.

00:04:25.440 --> 00:04:27.850
But you need to stick your chest out a little more,

00:04:27.850 --> 00:04:29.700
and position your hips like this—

00:04:29.700 --> 00:04:31.550
That's enough.

00:04:35.610 --> 00:04:36.480
Come on, man!

00:04:36.480 --> 00:04:40.050
Can't I help out an underclassman as the ace pitcher—

00:04:38.480 --> 00:04:40.050
I said, enough.

00:04:40.050 --> 00:04:43.570
Take the seventh-graders out for a run, Tsukishima.

00:04:43.570 --> 00:04:44.160
Got it.

00:04:44.580 --> 00:04:47.010
Ace pitcher, toss some pitches. I'll catch for you.

00:04:47.010 --> 00:04:49.100
Whatever you say, Captain.

00:04:55.160 --> 00:04:56.810
Ball.

00:05:32.200 --> 00:05:33.500
Yay, you got it!

00:05:33.500 --> 00:05:34.400
Isn't Daddy great?

00:05:34.400 --> 00:05:35.270
Yup!

00:05:35.270 --> 00:05:36.480
Ko!

00:05:39.390 --> 00:05:41.220
You seem bored, as usual.

00:05:42.070 --> 00:05:45.180
You won't get any girls unless you shape up, you know.

00:05:45.180 --> 00:05:46.420
Quiet, you.

00:05:46.420 --> 00:05:49.900
Elementary schoolers should treat middle schoolers with more respect!

00:05:49.900 --> 00:05:53.230
Then you'd better become a man who deserves my respect.

00:05:55.190 --> 00:05:57.260
Are you going home after swim class?

00:05:57.260 --> 00:05:58.350
I guess.

00:05:58.350 --> 00:06:00.470
Can you at least swim now?

00:06:00.470 --> 00:06:01.860
Can I <i>swim</i>?

00:06:01.860 --> 00:06:06.990
I took first place in the 50m freestyle at the fourth grade all-girls swimming competition, you know!

00:06:07.900 --> 00:06:09.610
My humble apologies.

00:06:09.610 --> 00:06:13.290
It was after two of the winning candidates dropped out, though.

00:06:13.290 --> 00:06:14.930
Who cares?

00:06:14.930 --> 00:06:16.420
First place is first place.

00:06:18.860 --> 00:06:22.260
Remember to treat girls nicely like that, Ko.

00:06:22.790 --> 00:06:24.800
Didn't I tell you to show some respect?

00:06:28.910 --> 00:06:30.270
Welcome back, Aoba.

00:06:30.270 --> 00:06:32.810
God, I'm starving.

00:06:32.810 --> 00:06:34.990
Give me something to eat, Sis.

00:06:34.990 --> 00:06:37.980
Did you pass Ko on your way here by any chance?

00:06:37.980 --> 00:06:39.450
He was here?

00:06:39.450 --> 00:06:40.410
Yeah.

00:06:40.410 --> 00:06:43.780
He brought Momiji back, but left just now.

00:06:43.780 --> 00:06:45.040
Where did he sit?

00:06:45.040 --> 00:06:47.420
The same seat you're sitting in right now.

00:06:48.760 --> 00:06:51.360
I'm starving.

00:06:51.360 --> 00:06:53.090
You still don't like him, huh?

00:06:53.590 --> 00:06:56.760
Wakaba liked him best, you know.

00:06:56.760 --> 00:06:57.900
That's exactly why.

00:07:08.160 --> 00:07:11.100
What are you working so hard on?

00:07:11.100 --> 00:07:13.100
I'm writing up a list of birthday presents I want,

00:07:13.100 --> 00:07:17.480
since Ko's having trouble picking out gifts for me.

00:07:20.630 --> 00:07:23.710
"Age 12, a cute brooch."

00:07:23.710 --> 00:07:26.930
"Age 13, cute sandals."

00:07:26.930 --> 00:07:30.190
"Age 14, a cute wallet."

00:07:30.190 --> 00:07:34.740
Ages 15, 16, 17, 18... earrings...

00:07:34.740 --> 00:07:36.630
Exactly how long is this list?

00:07:39.950 --> 00:07:43.140
Age 20... "engagement ring"?

00:07:45.220 --> 00:07:46.970
W-Wait a second, Waka!

00:07:46.970 --> 00:07:49.360
You want to marry a guy like <i>him</i>?

00:07:49.360 --> 00:07:50.380
Can't I?

00:07:50.380 --> 00:07:51.750
Of course not!

00:07:51.750 --> 00:07:55.330
That means he's going to become my brother-in-law!

00:07:55.330 --> 00:07:56.620
Of course he will.

00:07:56.620 --> 00:07:57.920
Forget that!

00:07:57.920 --> 00:08:00.190
I'll never approve of it! Over my dead body!

00:08:00.190 --> 00:08:02.590
Calm down.

00:08:02.590 --> 00:08:04.200
It's way in the future.

00:08:05.580 --> 00:08:09.530
More importantly, Aoba, what kind of guys do you like?

00:08:19.590 --> 00:08:22.780
A guy who can throw a 160km/h fastball.

00:08:33.320 --> 00:08:36.680
<i>A guy who can throw a 160km/h fastball.</i>

00:08:48.060 --> 00:08:49.540
Going out, Ko?

00:08:49.540 --> 00:08:51.620
I'm going to go to the bookstore in front of the station.

00:08:51.620 --> 00:08:54.550
Then take these balls over to the Tsukishimas while you're at it.

00:08:54.550 --> 00:08:56.230
That's in the opposite direction, though.

00:08:56.230 --> 00:08:57.440
Don't worry.

00:08:57.440 --> 00:08:59.590
The world is round, you know.

00:08:59.590 --> 00:09:01.250
You expect me to circle the world?!

00:09:02.150 --> 00:09:03.690
What's up, Kitamura?

00:09:03.690 --> 00:09:05.190
It's me.

00:09:05.190 --> 00:09:10.000
Senda Keiichiro, the Seishu Academy Middle School baseball team's ace pitcher and cleanup hitter.

00:09:10.000 --> 00:09:11.300
What are you up to?

00:09:11.300 --> 00:09:12.290
Nothing much.

00:09:12.290 --> 00:09:15.290
I'm going to go buy some manga over at the bookstore.

00:09:15.290 --> 00:09:16.970
What are <i>you</i> up to?

00:09:18.710 --> 00:09:21.790
What else would a hunk like me do on a Sunday besides going on a date?

00:09:21.790 --> 00:09:22.640
A date?

00:09:22.640 --> 00:09:23.610
Yeah.

00:09:23.610 --> 00:09:25.700
I'm sure you've at least seen her around.

00:09:25.700 --> 00:09:28.850
I'm going out with Tsukishima Aoba,
the eighth-grader from the baseball team.

00:09:28.850 --> 00:09:30.990
I asked her out to the movies over the phone.

00:09:30.990 --> 00:09:33.580
I told her I'd wait in front of the station at eleven.

00:09:33.580 --> 00:09:35.140
Did she say she'd actually come?

00:09:35.140 --> 00:09:36.460
You numbskull.

00:09:36.460 --> 00:09:38.790
I'm not going to sit around waiting for an answer all day.

00:09:38.790 --> 00:09:41.560
It's important to play these things cool.

00:09:41.560 --> 00:09:43.530
Besides, I can't imagine that any girl would refuse—

00:09:44.060 --> 00:09:46.400
Hey, Kitamura...

00:09:51.560 --> 00:09:53.440
Where's the old man?

00:09:53.440 --> 00:09:57.140
He is currently away from his office, and won't be back for some time.

00:09:59.410 --> 00:10:01.880
Then sign this for me.

00:10:07.430 --> 00:10:11.560
The old man usually gives me a token and tells me to take a few swings.

00:10:19.100 --> 00:10:21.000
I'd like my home run prize socks, please.

00:10:21.000 --> 00:10:22.640
Have you no shame?

00:10:22.640 --> 00:10:26.140
You really expect us to give you a prize for a free game you played?

00:10:26.140 --> 00:10:27.440
Is that how it is?

00:10:33.510 --> 00:10:35.490
That'll be three pairs.

00:10:38.880 --> 00:10:40.300
Oh yeah,

00:10:40.300 --> 00:10:42.400
didn't you have something to do today?

00:10:42.400 --> 00:10:44.990
Something to do? No, I don't.

00:10:46.100 --> 00:10:47.250
I see.

00:10:47.250 --> 00:10:49.430
Tell the old man I said hi, then.

00:10:55.700 --> 00:10:58.100
<i>Two balls to go with one more pair of socks to win.</i>

00:11:02.560 --> 00:11:03.580
Damn it!

00:11:03.580 --> 00:11:06.760
Hey, we need someone at the reception desk here!

00:11:06.760 --> 00:11:07.510
Coming!

00:11:08.000 --> 00:11:09.110
Oh geez,

00:11:09.110 --> 00:11:12.360
could you run over to Ko's for me, Aoba?

00:11:12.360 --> 00:11:13.450
What?!

00:11:28.800 --> 00:11:30.780
May I help you?

00:11:30.780 --> 00:11:32.330
Oh, please excuse me.

00:11:32.330 --> 00:11:34.810
Is Tsukishima Aoba here?

00:11:34.810 --> 00:11:36.270
What business do you have with Aoba?

00:11:36.270 --> 00:11:39.570
Are you Aoba's big sister by any chance?

00:11:39.570 --> 00:11:40.940
Yes.

00:11:40.940 --> 00:11:42.200
It's nice to meet you.

00:11:42.200 --> 00:11:44.150
I'm from Seishu Academy Middle School,

00:11:44.150 --> 00:11:45.680
and I am currently planning to go out—

00:11:48.250 --> 00:11:50.530
Oh my god, a cat!

00:11:50.530 --> 00:11:52.990
There's a cat here!

00:11:52.990 --> 00:11:55.220
Have you never seen one before?

00:11:56.520 --> 00:11:59.030
Well actually, today we were supposed to—

00:12:01.480 --> 00:12:04.170
What a doofus.

00:12:04.580 --> 00:12:06.860
Damn it, who was that little runt just now?

00:12:06.860 --> 00:12:09.540
That's Momiji, Aoba's little sister.

00:12:10.410 --> 00:12:12.820
So, what did you want with her?

00:12:12.820 --> 00:12:15.110
Oh, well, I...

00:12:17.050 --> 00:12:20.860
"Clover" is such a wonderful name!

00:12:20.860 --> 00:12:24.300
It rings full of happiness and love!

00:12:24.300 --> 00:12:26.430
Our mother came up with it before she died.

00:12:27.730 --> 00:12:31.120
She took it from our names, since there are four of us.

00:12:32.480 --> 00:12:35.830
One... two... three...

00:12:36.850 --> 00:12:37.300
Huh?

00:12:38.910 --> 00:12:40.710
Ichiyo,

00:12:40.710 --> 00:12:43.240
sorry to bother you, but could you make me a cup of coffee?

00:12:43.240 --> 00:12:46.070
Hey, Dad, do you know where Aoba went?

00:12:46.070 --> 00:12:51.150
Yeah, she went over to Ko's. I sent her over to deliver the mushrooms that came in from the countryside.

00:12:51.800 --> 00:12:53.500
So you're her father.

00:12:53.500 --> 00:12:56.920
I'm Seishu Academy Middle School baseball team's ace pitcher—

00:12:56.920 --> 00:12:59.050
Wait, Ko?

00:12:59.050 --> 00:12:59.800
Yeah.

00:12:59.800 --> 00:13:03.090
Kitamura Ko, the Seishu Academy Middle School ninth-grader.

00:13:04.780 --> 00:13:08.810
So how's the baseball team working out for you?

00:13:10.900 --> 00:13:13.560
Here you go, Aoba.

00:13:13.560 --> 00:13:15.150
Croquettes straight from the fryer.

00:13:15.150 --> 00:13:18.480
It's been so long since I've had your homemade croquettes, Mrs. Kitamura!

00:13:18.480 --> 00:13:21.560
I made a lot, so make sure to take some back home with you.

00:13:21.560 --> 00:13:23.410
They look so good!

00:13:23.410 --> 00:13:24.580
Thank you!

00:13:24.580 --> 00:13:25.940
Take your time eating them.

00:13:25.940 --> 00:13:27.190
Okay!

00:13:28.190 --> 00:13:30.460
So, how's it going with the baseball team?

00:13:30.460 --> 00:13:32.260
Shut up.

00:13:32.260 --> 00:13:34.390
That's none of your business.

00:13:34.390 --> 00:13:35.340
That's funny.

00:13:35.340 --> 00:13:38.800
I could have sworn that there was a nice, friendly girl here just now.

00:13:39.900 --> 00:13:41.700
Oh no, the sauce!

00:13:43.200 --> 00:13:46.020
It's going to stain!

00:13:46.020 --> 00:13:47.070
Here.

00:13:47.070 --> 00:13:49.940
I washed it, so it's not dirty or anything.

00:13:52.780 --> 00:13:54.060
Isn't this a little big for me?

00:13:54.060 --> 00:13:55.890
You'll have to make do with it.

00:13:55.890 --> 00:14:00.400
Ko, your friend Senda is here for you.

00:14:00.400 --> 00:14:02.690
My friend Senda?

00:14:06.110 --> 00:14:08.590
Damn you, Kitamura, you've been playing me all along!

00:14:08.590 --> 00:14:11.060
What's going on between you and Tsukishima? Spit it out!

00:14:12.020 --> 00:14:13.780
It's exactly what you think.

00:14:14.630 --> 00:14:17.710
We've just grown up in the same neighborhood, that's all.

00:14:17.710 --> 00:14:19.050
Really?

00:14:19.050 --> 00:14:22.040
That's what she says now, but yes, we're actually—

00:14:23.700 --> 00:14:26.330
I really like Mr. and Mrs. Kitamura,

00:14:26.330 --> 00:14:28.110
but I hate this guy!

00:14:28.850 --> 00:14:31.560
Thanks for having me over, Mrs. Kitamura!

00:14:31.560 --> 00:14:34.970
Don't forget to take some croquettes home, Aoba!

00:14:34.970 --> 00:14:36.490
Okay!

00:14:39.030 --> 00:14:41.490
She hates you, apparently.

00:14:41.490 --> 00:14:44.430
That's old news.

00:15:03.360 --> 00:15:06.180
I came to root for Aoba since she said she was pitching,

00:15:06.180 --> 00:15:08.010
but I didn't know she was playing against you guys!

00:15:08.010 --> 00:15:09.800
That's your sister, Tsukishima?

00:15:09.800 --> 00:15:12.410
Yup, she pitches pretty well, huh?

00:15:12.410 --> 00:15:15.390
"Pretty well" would be an understatement.

00:15:15.390 --> 00:15:16.640
Don't worry!

00:15:16.640 --> 00:15:19.360
We beat Akaishi and we can beat her!

00:15:19.360 --> 00:15:20.300
Right, Ko?

00:15:20.860 --> 00:15:21.850
Huh?

00:15:21.850 --> 00:15:23.230
Where's Ko?

00:15:23.230 --> 00:15:25.000
Listen, you guys!

00:15:25.000 --> 00:15:28.890
You only live once, so why not buy matching uniforms?

00:15:28.890 --> 00:15:33.280
We're actually holding a customer appreciation sale over at Kitamura Sports right now—

00:15:33.280 --> 00:15:34.570
The game's starting.

00:15:34.570 --> 00:15:36.550
You didn't have to kick me with your spikes, man.

00:15:37.610 --> 00:15:38.950
Play ball!

00:15:41.790 --> 00:15:43.220
Batter out!

00:15:43.220 --> 00:15:45.620
Third batter: Kitamura, pitcher!

00:15:51.400 --> 00:15:53.500
Go get 'em, Ko!

00:15:53.500 --> 00:15:54.930
Okay.

00:16:00.210 --> 00:16:01.070
Strike!

00:16:03.270 --> 00:16:04.180
All right.

00:16:11.600 --> 00:16:13.320
Foul ball!

00:16:13.320 --> 00:16:14.250
That was close!

00:16:16.050 --> 00:16:19.720
<i>I may have never played catch until recently,</i>

00:16:19.720 --> 00:16:22.070
<i>but I've been swinging the bat since I was three</i>

00:16:22.070 --> 00:16:23.930
<i>at Tsukishima Batting Center!</i>

00:16:28.210 --> 00:16:29.300
Hit by pitch!

00:16:30.500 --> 00:16:32.640
Ow...

00:16:40.080 --> 00:16:41.580
I got it!

00:16:42.760 --> 00:16:43.710
Yes.

00:16:43.710 --> 00:16:45.420
That's three outs! Change!

00:16:48.850 --> 00:16:50.720
Hit by pitch!

00:16:49.200 --> 00:16:50.720
Ow...

00:16:59.430 --> 00:17:01.570
That's three outs, change!

00:17:00.520 --> 00:17:01.570
Yeah.

00:17:04.170 --> 00:17:06.600
You having fun, pitching like that?

00:17:07.280 --> 00:17:10.460
I don't find baseball the least bit fun.

00:17:17.240 --> 00:17:20.250
How about you throw the ball a little harder next time?

00:17:20.250 --> 00:17:22.300
Is there a point?

00:17:22.300 --> 00:17:24.860
They haven't scored a run on us yet.

00:17:24.860 --> 00:17:27.460
Well, if that's what you want.

00:17:28.460 --> 00:17:29.860
Batter out!

00:17:29.860 --> 00:17:31.240
Way to go, Aoba!

00:17:31.240 --> 00:17:32.430
Keep it up!

00:17:32.430 --> 00:17:33.940
Come on, now!

00:17:33.940 --> 00:17:36.840
Go over to the other bench if you're going to root for your sister!

00:17:36.840 --> 00:17:39.990
I'm rooting for you when you're pitching, aren't I?

00:17:39.990 --> 00:17:42.140
Do you really expect me to run back and forth?

00:17:44.630 --> 00:17:45.470
Strike!

00:17:45.470 --> 00:17:46.960
Batter out!

00:17:54.250 --> 00:17:55.360
Two outs.

00:17:55.360 --> 00:17:56.690
Batter on first and third.

00:17:56.690 --> 00:17:58.620
Tsukishima at the plate!

00:18:00.020 --> 00:18:01.890
Good luck, Ko!

00:18:12.700 --> 00:18:13.260
Safe!

00:18:13.260 --> 00:18:15.640
Don't throw the ball, you won't make it!

00:18:13.260 --> 00:18:14.140
Yes!

00:18:16.770 --> 00:18:18.610
Just barely safe!

00:18:28.650 --> 00:18:30.590
Darn it!

00:18:30.990 --> 00:18:33.370
G-Good try.

00:18:36.870 --> 00:18:37.830
Balk!

00:18:37.830 --> 00:18:39.980
Ow...

00:18:44.540 --> 00:18:46.300
It's raining.

00:18:48.470 --> 00:18:50.240
Ow...

00:18:59.070 --> 00:19:01.020
He seemed pretty frustrated.

00:19:01.910 --> 00:19:02.860
About what?

00:19:02.860 --> 00:19:05.220
About losing to you.

00:19:05.220 --> 00:19:08.890
His looks may say otherwise, but Ko really hates losing.

00:19:08.890 --> 00:19:13.550
Ha! All this from the guy who can't even play catch properly.

00:19:13.550 --> 00:19:16.800
Don't think of Ko as just another boy!

00:19:17.160 --> 00:19:18.580
Once he gets serious,

00:19:18.580 --> 00:19:20.730
he could become the best pitcher in Japan!

00:19:20.730 --> 00:19:23.740
He might even be able to throw 160km/h.

00:19:26.320 --> 00:19:29.030
I don't think you believe me.

00:19:29.030 --> 00:19:31.730
My predictions tend to come true, you know.

00:19:33.060 --> 00:19:35.890
But even then, you can't steal him away from me, okay?

00:19:48.120 --> 00:19:52.270
Looks like your prediction was off, Waka.

00:20:02.500 --> 00:20:06.280
Why are you working out when you're not even in any of the sports teams?

00:20:06.280 --> 00:20:09.320
This is just a daily routine of mine.

00:20:10.160 --> 00:20:12.890
How long have you been keeping this up for?

00:20:15.040 --> 00:20:16.900
I forget.

00:20:17.920 --> 00:20:21.370
This is the training regimen Aoba follows every day.

00:20:23.220 --> 00:20:24.860
She does <i>this</i> every day?

00:20:24.860 --> 00:20:25.830
No way.

00:20:25.830 --> 00:20:28.340
Don't worry, you can do it, Ko.

00:20:28.340 --> 00:20:31.000
Weren't you frustrated that you lost to Aoba?

00:20:31.000 --> 00:20:32.790
She wouldn't get off your back after the game.

00:20:32.790 --> 00:20:35.520
She said your form was off, your back and legs were weak,

00:20:35.520 --> 00:20:37.980
and then she even said that you throw like a girl!

00:20:37.980 --> 00:20:41.500
Anyway, the fact still stands that she's talking crap about you behind your back!

00:20:41.500 --> 00:20:44.090
Sounds to me like you're more frustrated than I am.

00:20:44.090 --> 00:20:45.990
You can do it, Ko!

00:20:45.990 --> 00:20:47.990
Make Aoba swallow her words!

00:20:50.340 --> 00:20:54.130
I still don't get why Aoba hates me so much.

00:20:54.130 --> 00:20:56.880
It's not hard to get her to like you.

00:20:56.880 --> 00:21:00.100
You just need to be able to throw 160km/h.

00:21:00.100 --> 00:21:02.810
I guess that's "not hard" in terms of understanding what it is.

00:21:02.810 --> 00:21:03.970
Don't worry.

00:21:03.970 --> 00:21:05.490
I know you can do it, Ko.

00:23:11.200 --> 00:23:15.400
<i>Have you heard the rumors about the high school baseball team, Akaishi?</i>

00:23:15.400 --> 00:23:17.070
<i>Yeah, I've heard them.</i>

00:23:17.070 --> 00:23:18.170
<i>They're just rumors, right?</i>

00:23:18.170 --> 00:23:18.900
<i>Who knows.</i>

00:23:19.570 --> 00:23:21.300
<i>We're changing pitchers, Ref!</i>

00:23:21.300 --> 00:23:24.630
<i>Oh come on, Nakanishi, I was just warming up.</i>

00:23:24.630 --> 00:23:26.110
<i>Just when I thought I'd been missing sandlot games.</i>

00:23:26.110 --> 00:23:27.410
<i>Take right field, Ko.</i>

00:23:27.410 --> 00:23:29.880
<i>Just give me a little time!</i>

00:23:29.880 --> 00:23:32.580
<i>Next time, on Cross Game Episode Three:</i>

00:23:32.580 --> 00:23:33.980
<i>Hard?</i>

00:23:34.280 --> 00:23:38.470
<i>Why the hell didn't you join the baseball team when you can pitch like this?!</i>
